    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick, mini.extra\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.10.x\n\n### Description\n\nHi, thanks so much for making `mini.nvim`. I use it to replace a lot of plugins in my config recently and very love it!\n\nThe issue:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5a860aab-e65c-4fdb-8c65-df443053337b\n\n### Reproduction\n\n1. Create separate 'nvim-repro' config directory:\n    - '~/.config/nvim-repro/' on Unix\n    - '~/AppData/Local/nvim-repro/' on Windows\n\n2. Inside 'nvim-repro' directory create a file named 'init.lua'.\n   Populate it with the following content:\n\n```lua\nlocal lazypath = vim.fn.stdpath(\"data\") .. \"lazy/lazy.nvim\"\nif not vim.loop.fs_stat(lazypath) then\n    vim.fn.system({\n        \"git\",\n        \"clone\",\n        \"--filter=blob:none\",\n        \"https://github.com/folke/lazy.nvim.git\",\n        \"--branch=stable\", -- latest stable release\n        lazypath,\n    })\nend\nvim.opt.rtp:prepend(lazypath)\n\nrequire(\"lazy\").setup({\n    {\n        'echasnovski/mini.pick',\n        event = 'BufEnter',\n        version = '*',\n        dependencies = { \"echasnovski/mini.extra\" },\n\topts = {},\n        init = function()\n\t    require(\"mini.extra\").setup()\n        end\n    },\n    {\n        \"jake-stewart/multicursor.nvim\",\n        branch = \"1.0\",\n        event = \"BufReadPost\",\n        opts = {},\n    }\n})\n```\n\n3. In `nvim-repro` directory, run `NVIM_APPNAME=nvim-repro nvim init.lua` (i.e. execute `nvim` with `NVIM_APPNAME` environment variable set to \"nvim-repro\").\n   Wait for all dependencies to install.\n\n4. Run `:Pick keymaps` from command and search `gcc` then press enter. The line under cursor should be commented, but it is not.\n\nNote: after reporting the issue, it is safe (and even recommended for cleaner possible future bug reports) to remove 'nvim-repro' config from the system:\n- Delete config directory ('~/.config/nvim-repro' on Unix).\n- Delete data directory ('~/.local/share/nvim-repro' on Unix).\n- Delete state directory ('~/.local/state/nvim-repro' on Unix).\n",
